identical results here: classical MDS reconstructs coordinates from a
distance matrix by eigendecomposing its double-centered Gram matrix,
which -- when the distances are already exact Euclidean distances of a
coordinate set you have in hand, as they are for a fitted embedding --
is exactly the Gram matrix PCA operates on directly. MDS earns its keep
when you start from dissimilarities that are \emph{not} already known to
